Why CC0 for this artifact specifically
--------------------------------------

A schema is an interface. Maximum permissionless adoption is the entire point
of publishing it — any application in the Atmosphere must be able to emit or
read a com.beehivenature.receipt without asking anyone, without attribution
obligations, and without a license review.

CC0 is also what Bluesky chose for its own atproto interop test vectors, so
this matches the ecosystem's existing precedent for interface artifacts.

Note the scope boundary: CC0 covers THIS SCHEMA FILE only. Accompanying
reference implementations ship dual MIT / Apache-2.0, mirroring the atproto
reference implementation and carrying its patent grant. Do not read this
dedication as covering any code.
